2. Hamiltonian Bus Protocol (HBP) Specification
The Hamiltonian Bus Protocol (HBP) governs deterministic data transport between GPU compute clusters and FPGA symplectic accelerators, eliminating bus arbitration jitter.
 * Physical Layer: Optical-electrical SerDes channels operating at 112 Gbps per lane across a 64-bit parallel backplane.
 * Packet Framing: Fixed 512-byte frames structured for zero-copy direct memory access (DMA) into accelerator scratchpad memory.
 * Deterministic Arbitration: Token-ring priority scheduling guaranteeing maximum bus latency \tau_{\text{bus}} \le 150\text{ ns}.
 * Error Correction: Bose–Chaudhuri–Hocquenghem (BCH) error-correcting codes embedded in every transmission header to ensure 100% data integrity under high radiation and electromagnetic interference.
